----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE / PARITY
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RouteDisplay is a pure-presentational leaf: the web component's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`
(no query, no async, no loading/error/stale/offline). Its real, prop-driven render branches are
ALL reproduced natively, 1:1:
  • noLocation — neither endpoint resolved → muted "No location data".
  • single     — only `start` supplied (e.g. a charger) → label only, no round-trip suffix.
  • roundTrip  — start ≈ end (matching address OR coords within `roundTripThresholdM`) → label
                 + muted " ↻ round trip".
  • fromTo     — distinct endpoints → "{start} → {end}", each falling back to "No location data".
Helpers ported verbatim: endpointLabel (trimmed address, else `📍 lat, lon` @ toFixed(2), else nil)
and haversineMeters (R=6_371_000, asin clamp). The generic prompt "states" list (loading/error/
stale/offline) has NO web-source equivalent for this synchronous atom and is intentionally NOT
fabricated (would be drift). Data binding (P1/S8): the view performs NO I/O; it binds either the
web props directly or a cached history row via `RouteDisplayAdapter.input(from: RouteRowSnapshot)`
— the "cached → projection" seam unit-tested below. i18n (P1/S10): the two web keys
(route.noLocationData, route.roundTrip) + glyph-free VoiceOver keys resolve through
`RouteDisplayStrings` (table "RouteDisplay" → RouteDisplay.strings). Telemetry (P1/S11):
`view.opened surface=RouteDisplay` emitted once on first appear via an injectable seam. Tokens
(P1/S9): Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing only — no Tailwind ports, no raw hex. Charts/maps: none
in the web source, so none added.

